hello i'm zlatan i'm a third year  medical student studying at the  university of exeter and today i'm going  to share my study tips on how i ranked  first in my first year so i had the  highest end of year average amongst all  of my course mates  my first tip is planning planning  beforehand is very important because  when you put down every task that you  need to finish every topic that you need  to go through all the questions like how  many questions exactly in a very  detailed manner so you're more aware of  how much workload you have it will give  you a realistic idea of what you need to  do so that you can pass the exam seeing  all those tasks stuff that you need to  finish will stress you out a little bit  probably also it will push you you'll  actually realize the i guess seriousness  of the situation  so that you can study more and so that  you can plan your day ahead i usually  plan my day on the day because sometimes  life gets in the way if you plan your  whole month beforehand probably you  won't do the stuff that you've written  that day when the time comes because  there's always something that comes up  so my second tip is being comfortable  while you're studying being comfortable  really changes the game it lets you  enjoy the study process a lot more and  you can study for longer hours that way  if you're not comfortable in your seat  if you're in a really weird posture and  your back is hurting you're dehydrated  you're hungry the lighting is not great  the clothes that you're wearing are not  that comfortable then all i want to do  just jump to my bed and lie on my bed so  that my back can rest and i just want to  go on my phone so adjusting yourself  like trying to get to a comfortable  position rather than focusing on that  you want to focus on your work if for  example having a blanket around you  while you're studying is more  comfortable for you then do that as long  as it's not too comfortable that you  fall asleep most of the time i got my  blanket on if i'm studying in my room  bringing your laptop to your eye level  is also very helpful for the comfort of  your neck you can have some tea or water  with you basically whatever is going to  help with you feeling more cozy and  comfortable  using the same revision source is  important because it will help you  create a memory image for example a  specific powerpoint that your lecturer  has provided you on the notes that  you've found on the internet that you  found very helpful the next time you  revisit that topic go back to the same  revision source because whilst you  actually in an exam situation you're  trying to remember what was written in  that specific note that specific  information you're more likely to  remember you will be able to visualize  those notes that you went through  consistently rather than changing your  notes all the time because you revisited  that specific notes each time for you  more likely to remember the information  and so you're more likely to get the  answer right  my last step is not procrastinating and  actually get the work done if you like  to be on your phone via social media i  think phones are a big distractor for  that reason what i'd like to do before i  start my study session or study day i'd  like to put my phone on focus and  then put it in my wardrobe or somewhere  that i can't see my phone because even  seeing my phone can actually distract me  and also hearing those notifications can  be very distracting so just trying to  get rid of those distractors helps you  to sit down and get that work done and  procrastinate less  so thank you so much for watching this  video and if you found it helpful feel  free to subscribe and like this video  and if you want to know more about the  process that i went through to get into  medical school you can find that on my  channel as well thank you
 

